{{also|schaden}}
==German==

===Alternative form===
* {{l/de|Schade}} {{i|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|scado|lang=goh}}. Confer {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|schade|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|scathe|lang=en}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|skada|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaːdən/|[ˈʃaːdən]|[ˈʃaːdn̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schaden.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schadens|Schäden}}

# [[damage]]; [[harm]]
#: ''Das Auto hat einen '''Schaden.''''' - “The car is damaged.”
#: ''Er hat seiner Frau nie '''Schaden''' zugefügt.'' - “He has never done any harm to his wife.”
# {{context|colloquial|informal|lang=de}} [[mental]] [[problem]] {{qualifier|in the sense of “crazy”}}
#: ''Der hat doch ’n '''Schaden.''''' – “He must be out of his mind.''”

